{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/draft && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfb={\\\"ref_ids\\\":[\\\"S48-logger-fatal\\\",\\\"S22-replica-listener\\\",\\\"S3-run-dispatch\\\",\\\"S31-master-startup\\\"],\n \\\"answered\\\":\\\"A second attempt to exercise the replica's own event loop produced two facts and no clean measurement. First, with a single replica the loop still spends about ten seconds before serving: the peer-measurement phase performs twenty rounds with a half-second sleep each, and the panic trace in both attempts lands only after that interval. Second, in this execution environment the listen attempt fails and, because the harness uses a non-verbose logger, the logger's Fatal is silent - so the failure surfaces later as a nil-listener panic in the goroutine that waits for client connections, rather than as the clean exit the production launcher's verbose logger would produce. The measurement of the startup phase therefore could not be completed here: the loop cannot be kept alive long enough without a listener the environment permits, and the observation is recorded as construction knowledge with that environment caveat.\\\",\n \\\"remaining\\\":[\\\"a clean startup-phase measurement would need an environment that allows binding a local port, or a package-level injection point the implementation does not have\\\",\n   \\\"the reader-side and crash process-death steps remain inferences from the code (no recover in the loop, fatal only when verbose)\\\",\n   \\\"the two capacity-limited items, the two paused candidates, the configuration premises and the attribution issue remain as previously recorded\\\"],\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Recording the second failed construction keeps the environment limits and the silent-fatal behaviour visible without dressing them up as findings about the target, and it prevents a third attempt from repeating the same mistake.\\\",\n \\\"understanding\\\":\\\"updated\\\",\\\"question_updates\\\":{}}\nsub={\\\"action\\\":\\\"research\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Records the second loop-exercise attempt: the roughly ten-second startup phase is confirmed by the timing of both panics, and the environment's listen failure combined with a non-verbose logger turns a startup failure into a delayed nil-listener panic instead of a clean exit. No map object changes.\\\",\n \\\"feedback\\\":fb}\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-loop-note2.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('ok')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-loop-note2.json 2>&1 | head -6\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
